      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583282
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-19T00:15:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it make sense to just define this formally with the other `EV_` codes? That way if more `EV_` codes are added, `RUMBLE_EFFECT_TYPE` won\u0027t change values.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73080d8b_09eb58f4",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1683635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-21T19:25:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t move this with other EV codes because this feels like a hack (effects aren\u0027t supposed to be passed to the device through input events). This EV code is only relevant from this driver to CrosVm.",
      "parentUuid": "90e7fcef_8e8a75c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97c6a05b_94479e04",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583282
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-21T20:51:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, that makes sense (e.g. why clutter the rest of the code with it if it\u0027s just this driver).\n\nThe part I was thinking about is what might happen when we merge in upstream kernel changes, or migrate kernel versions. If there\u0027s a new EV code, we\u0027ll have to update the value on the CrosVM side too (and because this is a calculated macro, we can\u0027t see that value directly in the code).",
      "parentUuid": "73080d8b_09eb58f4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "124f13c3_39631979",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1683635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T22:51:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, that\u0027s a real concern. We can have the code start from `0xFFFF` so we are less likely to collide with new EV Codes.\n\nI don\u0027t know how difficult it would be to upstream these changes",
      "parentUuid": "97c6a05b_94479e04",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94ceeae3_6c821208",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583282
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T18:31:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 to `0xFFFF` (figuratively; literally would cause overflow).\n\nI suspect upstreaming will be pretty involved. We\u0027d have to add new input codes in the mainline kernel, modify the virtio spec, etc. So probably not something we should plan on near term.",
      "parentUuid": "124f13c3_39631979",
      "range": {
