      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583282
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-19T00:15:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we implement to let the device clean up effects / rumble settings that won\u0027t be used? (Presumably we have to store them on the device side since the kernel could write a dozen types of rumble settings before playing one of them.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 266,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 266,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d966cbf3_4d3ee809",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1683635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-21T19:25:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That sounds like what `virtinput_ff_erase` is supposed to do. `destroy`, from what I\u0027ve seen, is for drivers to deallocate memory they own, such as the `private` field in `ff_device`.\n\nSome drivers won\u0027t event implement `destroy` since they won\u0027t need it. I\u0027m logging callbacks that we won\u0027t necessarily need for debugging purposes.\n\nAlso when a vibration event takes place, [InputFlinger will upload to effect and then play it right after](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/services/inputflinger/reader/EventHub.cpp;l\u003d1634), so I don\u0027t think we need to save effects.",
      "parentUuid": "44811c65_3df8dd2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 266,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 266,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f4330f6_63a8c24b",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583282
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-21T20:54:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah gotcha, yeah that\u0027d be `virtinput_ff_erase` then.\n\nIt sounds like we wouldn\u0027t need to implement it at the moment, at least for what inputflinger does. It might be worth doing anyway for future proofing \u0026 completeness so we don\u0027t have to make more kernel changes later.",
      "parentUuid": "d966cbf3_4d3ee809",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 266,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 266,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e162e7e3_615da46c",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1683635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T22:51:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Without a plan on how KiwiVm will handle a `erase` request, it doesn\u0027t make sense to implement `virtinput_ff_erase`. One way to impl is by sending another input event type/code to the device, but we don\u0027t want to keep going down that path.",
      "parentUuid": "4f4330f6_63a8c24b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 266,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 266,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46a8dba9_94f72d47",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583282
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T18:31:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e One way to impl is by sending another input event type/code to the device, but we don\u0027t want to keep going down that path.\n\nHmm. Why would we want to avoid that path? Guest -\u003e device events are pretty rare, so we should have a lot of options?",
      "parentUuid": "e162e7e3_615da46c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 266,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 266,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "68996e6bced890874fb78ce387b750b333feb4d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d7d5ddf_6ba51e60",
        "filename": "drivers/virtio/virtio_input.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1683635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T20:23:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I only said because that will continue to hack virtio_input_event to be used for our specific purposes (ie. handling connection events). Then we need to create more custom event codes.\n\nI guess there isn\u0027t wrong with doing that, but that might be difficult to upstream, if we eventually want to.",
      "parentUuid": "46a8dba9_94f72d47",
